From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: skip CUDA language when SAPIEN_CUDA is off

Upstream-Status: To upstream [affects every non-CUDA Linux/Windows build, not riscv64-specific]

The top-level project() call enables CMake's CUDA language on every
platform except APPLE, independent of the SAPIEN_CUDA option. setup.py
passes -DSAPIEN_CUDA=OFF when CUDA_PATH is unset, and every CUDA use
further down (simsense, src/*.cu, CUDAToolkit, SVULKAN2_CUDA_INTEROP)
is already gated on it -- but project() runs first and makes CMake
require nvcc at configure time anyway ("Failed to find nvcc. Compiler
requires the CUDA toolkit."), so a CUDA-less build can never configure.

The -D cache value is already readable before project(), so key the
language list off it. When SAPIEN_CUDA is not set at all the option's
default (ON) is kept, so CUDA builds behave exactly as before.

Note that the system can't be tested by architecture here:
CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR (and CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR) are only set
by project() itself, so they are empty at this point.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18 FATAL_ERROR)
-if (APPLE)
+if (APPLE OR (DEFINED SAPIEN_CUDA AND NOT SAPIEN_CUDA))
     project(sapien LANGUAGES C CXX)
 else()
     project(sapien LANGUAGES C CXX CUDA)
--
